see ISO 1000;
*)

(*"measure_schema.si_unit_name.lumen"
see ISO 1000;
*)

(*"measure_schema.si_unit_name.lux"
see ISO 1000;
*)

(*"measure_schema.si_unit_name.becquerel"
see ISO 1000;
*)

(*"measure_schema.si_unit_name.gray"
see ISO 1000;
*)

(*"measure_schema.si_unit_name.sievert"
see ISO 1000.
*)

(*"measure_schema.solid_angle_measure"
A *solid\_angle\_measure* is the value of a solid angle.
*)

(*"measure_schema.thermodynamic_temperature_measure"
A *thermodynamic\_temperature\_measure* is the value for the degree of heat of a body.
*)

(*"measure_schema.time_measure"
A *time\_measure* is the value of the duration of a period.
*)

(*"measure_schema.unit"
A *unit* is a physical quantity, with a value of one. 

[NOTE]
--
A *unit* is used to express other physical quantities of the same kind.
--
*)

(*"measure_schema.velocity_measure"
A *velocity\_measure* is the value of the rate of change of position.
*)

(*"measure_schema.volume_measure"
A *volume\_measure* is the value of the solid content of a body.
*)

(*"measure_schema.absorbed_dose_measure_with_unit"
An *absorbed\_dose\_measure\_with\_unit* is a type of express_ref:[measure_schema.measure_with_unit] in which the physical quantity is an absorbed dose of radiation as defined in ISO 31.
*)

(*"measure_schema.absorbed_dose_measure_with_unit.wr:WR1"
The express_ref:[measure_schema.measure_with_unit.unit_component] be of type express_ref:[measure_schema.absorbed_dose_unit].
*)

(*"measure_schema.absorbed_dose_unit"
An *absorbed\_dose\_unit* is a type of express_ref:[measure_schema.derived_unit] in which the absorbed dose is expressed.
*)

(*"measure_schema.absorbed_dose_unit.wr:WR1"
The dimensional exponents shall be equal to those of the Gray as defined in ISO 31.
*)

(*"measure_schema.acceleration_measure_with_unit"
An *acceleration\_measure\_with\_unit* is a type of express_ref:[measure_schema.measure_with_unit] in which the physical quantity is an acceleration.
*)

(*"measure_schema.acceleration_measure_with_unit.wr:WR1"
The express_ref:[measure_schema.measure_with_unit.unit_component] be of type express_ref:[measure_schema.acceleration_unit].
*)

(*"measure_schema.acceleration_unit"
An *acceleration\_unit* is a type of express_ref:[measure_schema.derived_unit] in which the acceleration of an object is expressed.
*)

(*"measure_schema.acceleration_unit.wr:WR1"
The dimensional exponent of length shall be equal to one, the dimensional exponent of time shall be equal to minus two, and all the other dimensional exponents shall be equal to zero.
*)

(*"measure_schema.amount_of_substance_measure_with_unit"
An *amount\_of\_substance\_measure\_with\_unit* is a type of express_ref:[measure_schema.measure_with_unit]. 
// in which the physical quantity is an 
// <express_ref linkend="measure_schema:ir_express:measure_schema.amount_of_substance"/> 
// as defined in ISO 31.
 This entity data type shall only be used to characterize a number of particles.
*)

(*"measure_schema.amount_of_substance_measure_with_unit.wr:WR1"
The unit shall be an express_ref:[measure_schema.amount_of_substance_unit].
*)

(*"measure_schema.amount_of_substance_unit"
An *amount\_of\_substance\_unit* is a type of express_ref:[measure_schema.named_unit] in which the number of elementary entities of a substance as compared to the number of atoms in 0.012 kilograms of carbon-12 is expressed. 

[NOTE]
--
This definition applies to the SI quantity 'mole'. When the mole is used, the elementary entities, whose quantity is expressed, must be specified. They may be atoms, molecules, ions, electrons or other particles or specified groups of such particles (see ISO 31-8).
--

[NOTE]
--
This unit corresponds to one of the seven fundamental quantities as specified in ISO 1000.
--
*)

(*"measure_schema.amount_of_substance_unit.wr:WR1"
The dimensional exponent of amount of substance shall be equal to one, and all the other dimensional exponents shall be equal to zero.
*)

(*"measure_schema.area_measure_with_unit"
An *area\_measure\_with\_unit* is a type of express_ref:[measure_schema.measure_with_unit] in which the physical quantity is an area as defined in ISO 31.
*)

(*"measure_schema.area_measure_with_unit.wr:WR1"
The unit shall be an express_ref:[measure_schema.area_unit].
*)

(*"measure_schema.area_unit"
An *area\_unit* is a type of express_ref:[measure_schema.derived_unit] used to measure the extent of a surface.
*)

(*"measure_schema.area_unit.wr:WR1"
The dimensional exponent of length shall be equal to two and all the other dimensional exponents shall be equal to zero.
*)

(*"measure_schema.capacitance_measure_with_unit"
A *capacitance\_measure\_with\_unit* is a type of express_ref:[measure_schema.measure_with_unit] in which the physical quantity is an electric capacitance as defined in ISO 31.
*)

(*"measure_schema.capacitance_measure_with_unit.wr:WR1"
The express_ref:[measure_schema.measure_with_unit.unit_component] be of type express_ref:[measure_schema.capacitance_unit].
*)

(*"measure_schema.capacitance_unit"
A *capacitance\_unit* is a type of express_ref:[measure_schema.derived_unit] in which the capacitance is expressed.
*)

(*"measure_schema.capacitance_unit.wr:WR1"
The dimensional exponents shall be equal to those of the farad as defined in ISO 31.
*)

(*"measure_schema.celsius_temperature_measure_with_unit"
A *celsius\_temperature\_measure\_with\_unit* is a type of express_ref:[measure_schema.measure_with_unit] in which the physical quantity is a Celsius temperature as defined in ISO 31-4.
*)

(*"measure_schema.celsius_temperature_measure_with_unit.wr:WR1"
The unit shall be a express_ref:[measure_schema.thermodynamic_temperature_unit].
*)

(*"measure_schema.conductance_measure_with_unit"
A *conductance\_measure\_with\_unit* is a type of express_ref:[measure_schema.measure_with_unit] in which the physical quantity is a conductance as defined in ISO 31.
*)

(*"measure_schema.conductance_measure_with_unit.wr:WR1"
The express_ref:[measure_schema.measure_with_unit.unit_component] shall be of type express_ref:[measure_schema.conductance_unit].
*)

(*"measure_schema.conductance_unit"
A *conductance\_unit* is a type of express_ref:[measure_schema.derived_unit] in which the electrical conductance is expressed.
*)

(*"measure_schema.conductance_unit.wr:WR1"
The dimensional exponents shall be equal to those of the siemens as defined in ISO 31.
*)

(*"measure_schema.context_dependent_unit"
A *context\_dependent\_unit* is a type of express_ref:[measure_schema.named_unit] that is not related to the system of units defined in this part of ISO 10303. 

[example]
====
The number of parts in an assembly is a physical quantity that may be measured in a unit called “parts”. Such a unit cannot be related to an SI unit.
====
*)

(*"measure_schema.context_dependent_unit.name"
the express_ref:[support_resource_schema.label] by which the *context\_dependent\_unit* is known.
*)

(*"measure_schema.conversion_based_unit"
A *conversion\_based\_unit* is a type of express_ref:[measure_schema.named_unit] that defines a unit on the basis of a express_ref:[measure_schema.measure_with_unit]. 

[NOTE]
--
The express_ref:[measure_schema.measure_with_unit.value_component] attribute of the express_ref:[measure_schema.measure_with_unit] defines the conversion factor.
--

[example]
====
An inch is a *conversion\_based\_unit*. It is from the Imperial system, its name is "inch", and it can be related to the express_ref:[measure_schema.si_unit], millimetre, through a express_ref:[measure_schema.measure_with_unit] whose value is 25.4 millimetre. A foot is also a *conversion\_based\_unit*. It is from the Imperial system, its name is "foot", and it can be related to an express_ref:[measure_schema.si_unit], millimetre, either directly or through the unit called "inch".
====
*)

(*"measure_schema.conversion_based_unit.name"
the express_ref:[support_resource_schema.label] by which the *conversion\_based\_unit* is known.
*)

(*"measure_schema.conversion_based_unit.conversion_factor"
the express_ref:[measure_schema.measure_with_unit] that specifies the physical quantity from which the *conversion\_based\_unit* is derived.
*)

(*"measure_schema.conversion_based_unit.wr:WR1"
The dimensional exponents shall be equal to those from the express_ref:[measure_schema.conversion_based_unit.conversion_factor].
*)

(*"measure_schema.derived_unit"
A *derived\_unit* is an expression of units. 

[example]
====
Newtons per square millimetre is a *derived\_unit*.
====

 A *derived\_unit* may be either an express_ref:[measure_schema.absorbed_dose_unit] or an express_ref:[measure_schema.acceleration_unit], or a express_ref:[measure_schema.radioactivity_unit], or an express_ref:[measure_schema.area_unit], or a express_ref:[measure_schema.capacitance_unit], or a express_ref:[measure_schema.dose_equivalent_unit], or an express_ref:[measure_schema.electric_charge_unit], or a express_ref:[measure_schema.conductance_unit], or an express_ref:[measure_schema.electric_potential_unit], or an express_ref:[measure_schema.energy_unit], or a express_ref:[measure_schema.magnetic_flux_density_unit] or a express_ref:[measure_schema.force_unit], or a express_ref:[measure_schema.frequency_unit], or an express_ref:[measure_schema.illuminance_unit], or an express_ref:[measure_schema.inductance_unit], or a express_ref:[measure_schema.magnetic_flux_unit], or a express_ref:[measure_schema.power_unit], or a express_ref:[measure_schema.pressure_unit], or a express_ref:[measure_schema.resistance_unit], or a express_ref:[measure_schema.velocity_unit], or a express_ref:[measure_schema.volume_unit].
*)

(*"measure_schema.derived_unit.elements"
the express_ref:[measure_schema.derived_unit_element]s and their exponents that define the *derived\_unit*.
*)

(*"measure_schema.derived_unit.name"
the label by which the *derived\_unit* is known.

[NOTE]
--
This attribute is an upwardly compatible addition to *derived\_unit* as specified in ISO 10303-41:1994.
--
*)

(*"measure_schema.derived_unit.wr:WR1"
There shall be either more than one member in the elements set or the value of the exponent of the single element of the elements set shall not be equal to one.
*)

(*"measure_schema.derived_unit.wr:WR2"
Each *derived\_unit* shall be the express_ref:[basic_attribute_schema.name_attribute.named_item] in at most one express_ref:[basic_attribute_schema.name_attribute].

[NOTE]
--
The express_ref:[basic_attribute_schema.name_attribute] data type is defined in express_ref:[basic_attribute_schema] of this part of ISO 10303.
--

[NOTE]
--
A template for constraining the population of the entity data types defined in the express_ref:[basic_attribute_schema] is described in annex E.
--
*)

(*"measure_schema.derived_unit_element"
A *derived\_unit\_element* is the association of a express_ref:[measure_schema.named_unit] with an exponent. 

[NOTE]
--
This entity is used in this part of ISO 10303 to represent an element of the dimensional expression of a express_ref:[measure_schema.derived_unit].
--

[example]
====
Newtons per square millimetre is a derived unit. It has two elements, Newton whose exponent has a value of 1, and millimetre whose exponent is -2.
====
*)

(*"measure_schema.derived_unit_element.unit"
the express_ref:[measure_schema.named_unit] that specifies the mathematical factor of the element.
*)

(*"measure_schema.derived_unit_element.exponent"
the power that is applied to the unit attribute.
*)

(*"measure_schema.dimensional_exponents"
A *dimensional\_exponents* is a definition of the powers of the dimensions of the seven base quantities. 

[NOTE]
--
The seven base quantities are defined in ISO 31.
--

[NOTE]
--
This entity enables the dimensional expression of any physical quantity with respect to these seven base quantities.
--

[NOTE]
--
Length, mass, time, electric current, thermodynamic temperature, amount of substance, and luminous intensity are the seven base quantities.
--

[example]
====
A length of 2 millimetres has a length exponent of 1. The remaining exponents are equal to 0.
====

[example]
====
A velocity of 2 millimetres per second has a length exponent of 1 and a time exponent of -1. The remaining exponents are 0.
====
*)

(*"measure_schema.dimensional_exponents.length_exponent"
the power of the length base quantity.
*)

(*"measure_schema.dimensional_exponents.mass_exponent"
the power of the mass base quantity.
*)

(*"measure_schema.dimensional_exponents.time_exponent"
the power of the time base quantity.
*)

(*"measure_schema.dimensional_exponents.electric_current_exponent"
the power of the electric current base quantity.
*)

(*"measure_schema.dimensional_exponents.thermodynamic_temperature_exponent"
the power of the thermodynamic temperature base quantity.
*)

(*"measure_schema.dimensional_exponents.amount_of_substance_exponent"
the power of the amount of substance base quantity.
*)

(*"measure_schema.dimensional_exponents.luminous_intensity_exponent"
the power of the luminous intensity base quantity.
*)

(*"measure_schema.dose_equivalent_measure_with_unit"
A *dose\_equivalent\_measure\_with\_unit* is a type of express_ref:[measure_schema.measure_with_unit] in which the physical quantity is a radiation dose equivalent as defined in ISO 31.
*)

(*"measure_schema.dose_equivalent_measure_with_unit.wr:WR1"
The express_ref:[measure_schema.measure_with_unit.unit_component] shall be of type express_ref:[measure_schema.dose_equivalent_unit].
*)

(*"measure_schema.dose_equivalent_unit"
A *dose\_equivalent\_unit* is a type of express_ref:[measure_schema.derived_unit] in which the radiation dose equivalent is expressed.
*)

(*"measure_schema.dose_equivalent_unit.wr:WR1"
The dimensional exponents shall be equal to those of the sievert as defined in ISO 31.
*)

(*"measure_schema.electric_charge_measure_with_unit"
An *electric\_charge\_measure\_with\_unit* is a type of express_ref:[measure_schema.measure_with_unit] in which the physical quantity is an electric charge as defined in ISO 31.
*)

