(*"measure_schema.si_magnetic_flux_unit.wr:WR2"
No other name shall be assigned to this entity.
*)

(*"measure_schema.si_power_unit"
A *si\_power\_unit* is a type of express_ref:[measure_schema.power_unit] and a type of express_ref:[measure_schema.si_unit] in which the power is expressed in SI units.
*)

(*"measure_schema.si_power_unit.wr:WR1"
The express_ref:[measure_schema.si_unit.name] of the express_ref:[measure_schema.si_unit] shall be watt.
*)

(*"measure_schema.si_power_unit.wr:WR2"
No other name shall be assigned to this entity.
*)

(*"measure_schema.si_pressure_unit"
A *si\_pressure\_unit* is a type of express_ref:[measure_schema.pressure_unit] and a type of express_ref:[measure_schema.si_unit] in which the pressure is expressed in SI units.
*)

(*"measure_schema.si_pressure_unit.wr:WR1"
The express_ref:[measure_schema.si_unit.name] of the express_ref:[measure_schema.si_unit] shall be pascal.
*)

(*"measure_schema.si_pressure_unit.wr:WR2"
No other name shall be assigned to this entity.
*)

(*"measure_schema.si_radioactivity_unit"
A *si\_radioactivity\_unit* is a type of express_ref:[measure_schema.radioactivity_unit] and a type of express_ref:[measure_schema.si_unit] in which the radioactivity is expressed in SI units.
*)

(*"measure_schema.si_radioactivity_unit.wr:WR1"
The express_ref:[measure_schema.si_unit.name] of the express_ref:[measure_schema.si_unit] shall be becquerel.
*)

(*"measure_schema.si_radioactivity_unit.wr:WR2"
No other name shall be assigned to this entity.
*)

(*"measure_schema.si_resistance_unit"
A *si\_resistance\_unit* is a type of express_ref:[measure_schema.resistance_unit] and a type of express_ref:[measure_schema.si_unit] in which the resistance is expressed in SI units.
*)

(*"measure_schema.si_resistance_unit.wr:WR1"
The express_ref:[measure_schema.si_unit.name] of the express_ref:[measure_schema.si_unit] shall be ohm.
*)

(*"measure_schema.si_resistance_unit.wr:WR2"
No other name shall be assigned to this entity.
*)

(*"measure_schema.si_unit"
An *si\_unit* is a type of express_ref:[measure_schema.named_unit] that defines a unit with respect to the system of units defined in ISO 80000.
*)

(*"measure_schema.si_unit.prefix"
the express_ref:[measure_schema.si_prefix] that specifies the ratio with the unit specified by name. The value of this attribute need not be specified.
*)

(*"measure_schema.si_unit.name"
the express_ref:[measure_schema.si_unit_name] by which the *si\_unit* is known.
*)

(*"measure_schema.si_unit.dimensions"
the express_ref:[measure_schema.dimensional_exponents] for the *si\_unit*.
*)

(*"measure_schema.si_unit.wr:WR1"
If the *si\_unit* is a express_ref:[measure_schema.mass_unit] it shall not be used by a express_ref:[measure_schema.derived_unit_element] unless the prefix is express_ref:[measure_schema.si_prefix.kilo].
*)

(*"measure_schema.solid_angle_measure_with_unit"
A *solid\_angle\_measure\_with\_unit* is a type of express_ref:[measure_schema.measure_with_unit] in which the physical quantity is a solid angle as defined in ISO 31.
*)

(*"measure_schema.solid_angle_measure_with_unit.wr:WR1"
The unit shall be a express_ref:[measure_schema.solid_angle_unit].
*)

(*"measure_schema.solid_angle_unit"
A *solid\_angle\_unit* is a type of express_ref:[measure_schema.named_unit] in which solid angles are expressed.
*)

(*"measure_schema.solid_angle_unit.wr:WR1"
All the dimensional exponents shall be equal to zero.
*)

(*"measure_schema.thermodynamic_temperature_measure_with_unit"
A *thermodynamic\_temperature\_measure\_with\_unit* is a type of express_ref:[measure_schema.measure_with_unit] in which the physical quantity is a thermodynamic temperature as defined in ISO 31.
*)

(*"measure_schema.thermodynamic_temperature_measure_with_unit.wr:WR1"
The unit shall be a express_ref:[measure_schema.thermodynamic_temperature_unit].
*)

(*"measure_schema.thermodynamic_temperature_unit"
A *thermodynamic\_temperature\_unit* is a type of express_ref:[measure_schema.named_unit] in which the degree of heat of a body is expressed. 

[NOTE]
--
This unit corresponds to one of the seven fundamental quantities as specified in ISO 1000.
--
*)

(*"measure_schema.thermodynamic_temperature_unit.wr:WR1"
The dimensional exponent of thermodynamic temperature shall be equal to one and the other dimensional exponents shall be equal to zero.
*)

(*"measure_schema.time_measure_with_unit"
A *time\_measure\_with\_unit* is a type of express_ref:[measure_schema.measure_with_unit] in which the physical quantity is a time as defined in ISO 31.
*)

(*"measure_schema.time_measure_with_unit.wr:WR1"
The unit shall be a express_ref:[measure_schema.time_unit].
*)

(*"measure_schema.time_unit"
A *time\_unit* is a type of express_ref:[measure_schema.named_unit] in which the duration of periods is expressed. 

[NOTE]
--
This unit corresponds to one of the seven fundamental quantities as specified in ISO 1000.
--
*)

(*"measure_schema.time_unit.wr:WR1"
The dimensional exponent of time shall be equal to one, and all the other dimensional exponents shall be equal to zero.
*)

(*"measure_schema.velocity_measure_with_unit"
A *velocity\_measure\_with\_unit* is a type of express_ref:[measure_schema.measure_with_unit] in which the quantity measured is a velocity.
*)

(*"measure_schema.velocity_measure_with_unit.wr:WR1"
The express_ref:[measure_schema.measure_with_unit.unit_component] shall be of type express_ref:[measure_schema.velocity_unit].
*)

(*"measure_schema.velocity_unit"
A *velocity\_unit* is a type of express_ref:[measure_schema.derived_unit] in which the velocity is expressed.
*)

(*"measure_schema.velocity_unit.wr:WR1"
The dimensional exponent of length shall be equal to one, the dimensional exponent of time shall be equal to minus one, and all the other dimensional exponents shall be equal to zero.
*)

(*"measure_schema.volume_measure_with_unit"
A *volume\_measure\_with\_unit* is a type of express_ref:[measure_schema.measure_with_unit] in which the physical quantity is a volume as defined in ISO 31.
*)

(*"measure_schema.volume_measure_with_unit.wr:WR1"
The unit shall be a express_ref:[measure_schema.volume_unit].
*)

(*"measure_schema.volume_unit"
A *volume\_unit* is a type of express_ref:[measure_schema.derived_unit] used to measure the extent of a solid.
*)

(*"measure_schema.volume_unit.wr:WR1"
The dimensional exponent of length shall be equal to three and all the other dimensional exponents shall be equal to zero.
*)

(*"measure_schema.derive_dimensional_exponents"
The *derive\_dimensional\_exponents* function determines the dimensional exponents of a unit. For named units the dimensions attribute is returned and for derived units the dimensional exponents are calculated from its elements.
*)

(*"measure_schema.derive_dimensional_exponents.x"
(input) the express_ref:[measure_schema.unit] that the express_ref:[measure_schema.dimensional_exponents] are being derived from.
*)

(*"measure_schema.dimensions_for_si_unit"
The *dimensions\_for\_si\_unit* function returns the express_ref:[measure_schema.dimensional_exponents] of the given express_ref:[measure_schema.si_unit].
*)

(*"measure_schema.dimensions_for_si_unit.n"
(input) the name of the express_ref:[measure_schema.si_unit_name] for which the express_ref:[measure_schema.dimensional_exponents] will be returned.
*)

(*"measure_schema.valid_units"
The *valid\_units* function validates a express_ref:[measure_schema.measure_with_unit]. If the unit of the express_ref:[measure_schema.measure_with_unit] is valid the function returns TRUE. Otherwise, it returns FALSE.
*)

(*"measure_schema.valid_units.m"
(input) the candidate express_ref:[measure_schema.measure_with_unit] that is to be checked.
*)
